id: pm-w7ccmv
title: "Outcome milestone: provable history — every mutation immutably recorded, independently verifiable, restorable to any version"
description: "Outcome milestone for independently verifiable history: every item and workspace mutation is append-only, hash-verifiable, attributable, portable, and restorable to any version."
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: audit,history,"horizon:mid",immutability,integrity,milestone,outcome
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:43:21.135Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T21:27:59.810Z"
deadline: "2027-03-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 5400
acceptance_criteria: "A contract-driven gate proves every mutating CLI and SDK action appends a history entry, with zero exemptions outside a reviewed waiver ledger; Workspace-scoped mutations (schema/config/profile/init) write to an append-only audit stream; A detached hash-chain proof bundle exports and verifies standalone, without the workspace; Per-entry author attribution is verifiable rather than self-asserted, and unknown-author events are rejected under strict mode; Restore-to-any-version and point-in-time reads hold across compaction, redaction, repair, and merge"
goal: provable-history
objective: "Any third party can verify that the recorded history of any workspace was never altered, and any item can be reconstructed at any point in time"
value: "Immutable, verifiable proof is what makes an agent-written tracker trustworthy: without it, thousands of autonomous mutations are unauditable assertions."
impact: "Precondition for organizational adoption, for policy enforcement, and for any regulated or contractual use of pm as the system of record."
outcome: "Zero mutating actions bypass the history stream, per-entry authorship is attributable, and a detached proof bundle verifies standalone."
why_now: "Workspace-scoped mutations (schema, config, profile, init) still leave no append-only record, so the every-mutation-leaves-proof invariant is not yet true."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
